	"name": "Spell Composer",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/tools/instruments/lute-gold-brown.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You have begun to dabble with magic outside the scope of what most bards learn, but you have not neglected your artistic roots. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p>Your Strength, Wisdom, or Charisma increases by 1, to a maximum of 20.</p></li><li><p>You gain an expertise die to your Performance skill. Your maximum expertise die size for Performance increases to a d10. </p></li><li><p>You gain proficiency with a musical instrument of your choice.</p></li><li><p>You gain proficiency with a gaming set of your choice, disguise kits, forgery kits, navigator’s tools, or thieves’ tools.</p></li><li><p>You learn a 1st- or 2nd- level spell from the bard, cleric, or warlock list. It counts as a bard spell for you, and does not count against your spells known.</p></li><li><p>You learn an additional battle hymn from the 5th-8th list. It does not count against your battle hymns known.</p></li></ul>",
